  "title": "Last Order",
  "tagline": "A food critic with a deadly allergy, a one-star review, and a takeaway that killed him.",
  "setting": "Hackney · East London · March 2024",
  "sketchTitle": "HACKNEY",
  "sketchCredit": "SKETCH: SITE VISIT, 11 MARCH 2024 · NOT TO SCALE",
  "stayLabel": "Stay in Hackney",
  "briefing": [
    "Hackney, East London. Monday 11 March 2024, nine o’clock in the morning.",
    "Last Thursday night Jonah Pryce — thirty-four, 1.3 million followers, the most feared food critic on the internet — ordered a takeaway from a restaurant he had torn apart in January. He had a severe peanut allergy, and said so on the order. At 21:29 he posted himself taking the first spoonful. By 22:19 he was dead.",
    "A lab found peanut in the curry. Thambi’s chef-owner, Priya Ratnam, has been arrested on suspicion of manslaughter, her restaurant is shut, and half the internet has already convicted her. She swears her kitchen is nut-free.",
    "Her solicitors have hired you to find out what really happened. Jonah’s fiancée has given you the code to the flat. Everyone involved, she says, has been lying to the police about something.",
    "Find out who killed Jonah Pryce, how it was done and why — and be ready to prove it."
  ],
